[hermes:err-live] #### Issue body
[hermes:err-live] Rework of #51724, which was reverted in #51872. Rebased on post-revert master.
[hermes:err-live] ## What / why
[hermes:err-live] The same StorageV3 segment manifest is advanced concurrently by several producers — an external-collection refresh column patch, a sort-stats result, and a text/JSON index build. They adopted a result by a *version-newer* check only, without verifying it was built on the segment's **current** manifest, so a later write could silently overwrite a concurrent commit (lost update). Audit: #51723.
[hermes:err-live] ## Unchanged from #51724
[hermes:err-live] - **`base == current` CAS at the adoption sites.** A result is adopted only when the manifest it was built on still equals the segment's current manifest. The refresh CAS runs **inside** the `UpdateSegmentsInfo` / `segMu` critical section (in the upsert operator, via the synchronized `modPack.Get`) so the decision is atomic with the patch.
[hermes:err-live] - **Adopt only a legal *successor*.** A matching base is not sufficient — a buggy / mixed-version / corrupt worker could carry the right base yet a result pointing at another segment or an older version. Extracted into the shared `validateManifestSuccessor` so the refresh and schema-bump paths cannot drift.
[hermes:err-live] - **Rebuild on conflict**, refresh task failure classification, and "a task the worker no longer tracks re-dispatches rather than fails".
[hermes:err-live] ## Redesigned (the revert's two design objections)
[hermes:err-live] ### 1. Task registration rejects instead of evicting
[hermes:err-live] #51724 carried `task_version` on the wire so a re-dispatch could evict the resident attempt, with a version guard dropping the evicted attempt's late writes. That was the only worker in the tree with evict-on-conflict semantics.
[hermes:err-live] Registration now **rejects** a dispatch onto an occupied taskID with `ErrTaskDuplicate`, matching `LoadOrStoreIndexTask` / `LoadOrStoreStatsTask`. DataCoord drops the resident attempt before re-dispatching — which the create path already did, and which is now load-bearing rather than best-effort. This removes the class of stale write instead of guarding against it, and takes the version off the wire entirely.
[hermes:err-live] Why eviction forces a version to exist: eviction cancels the resident attempt, and a cancelled attempt's *partial* result then has to be fenced out of the entry the new attempt owns. Rejection leaves the resident attempt running to completion, so its result is never partial.
[hermes:err-live] The attempt version stays on the persisted task record, where it still fences DataCoord's own attempt-scoped meta writes (`UpdateTaskState` / `ResetTaskForRetry`).
[hermes:err-live] ### 2. Result writes go through the attempt's own handle
[hermes:err-live] Rejecting alone still leaves a window: a drop detaches the entry, the re-dispatch registers a fresh one under the same taskID, and the cancelled attempt's late write resolves the key to the *new* attempt. Writes now go through the `*TaskInfo` the attempt registered rather than a `(clusterID, taskID)` lookup, so a detached attempt writes into an object nobody reads.
[hermes:err-live] ### 3. `base_manifest` moves off the segment entity
[hermes:err-live] #51724 added `base_manifest` to `SegmentInfo` — the segment entity — with a comment stating it must never be set on a persisted live segment. It is an adoption token belonging to the result, as it already is for `StatsResult.base_manifest` and `CompactionSegment.base_manifest`.
[hermes:err-live] The result now has its own message carrying only what the worker produced:
[hermes:err-live] ```proto
[hermes:err-live] message ExternalRefreshSegmentResult {
[hermes:err-live]   int64 segment_id = 1;
[hermes:err-live]   string manifest = 2;
[hermes:err-live]   string base_manifest = 3;   // adoption token; empty for a new segment
[hermes:err-live]   int64 num_rows = 4;
[hermes:err-live]   int64 storage_version = 5;
[hermes:err-live]   int32 schema_version = 6;
[hermes:err-live]   repeated FieldBinlog binlogs = 7;
[hermes:err-live] }
[hermes:err-live] ```
[hermes:err-live] DataCoord materializes the `SegmentInfo` itself, so collection / partition / channel / state / level are no longer worker-supplied. A collection mismatch became **unrepresentable** rather than rejected at runtime.
[hermes:err-live] `SegmentInfo.base_manifest` and `RefreshExternalCollectionTaskRequest.task_version` are dropped from the proto. Both were introduced by #51724 and are reverte…
