[review] ### Summary
[review] This PR implements `base == current` CAS (compare-and-swap) for adopted sort-stats results and external-refresh manifest patches. It is a rework of #51724 (reverted in #51872) with two design changes: task registration rejects duplicates instead of evicting, and `base_manifest` moves off `SegmentInfo` onto coordinator-owned attempt records (`StatsTask.dispatched_manifest`, `ExternalCollectionRefreshTask.BaseManifests`). The core adoption now requires both that the worker built on the segment's current manifest AND that the result is a legal forward successor. The PR adds extensive test coverage (table-driven, race-condition scenario, cross-segment sort, old-DataNode fence) across all 46 files.
[review] 
